# GETSET admin. Copy to .env.local for development. All values are server-only.
# Both are required for a production build or server (`next build`, `next start`, Vercel): it stops with an error
# if one is missing or malformed, and on Vercel unless both are public https:// addresses. Only `next dev` falls
# back to the localhost values below. On Vercel, set both for the Production and Preview environments.

# The GETSET API (getset-itinerary-backend). The browser never calls it directly:
# the admin's server does, with the signed-in user's session token.
API_URL=http://localhost:4000

# The customer website, for "View on site" links.
SITE_URL=http://localhost:3000

# Shared with the API: must be the same value as its ADMIN_PROXY_SECRET on Render. On Vercel the admin's server uses it to
# tell the API which visitor a sign-in comes from, so each person has their own rate limit. Required on Vercel
# (Production and Preview); at least 32 characters; generate with: openssl rand -base64 48. Never a NEXT_PUBLIC_
# variable. Leave it unset for local development: nothing is passed on outside Vercel.
# ADMIN_PROXY_SECRET=
